  {
   "id": "note--02267fca-8aea-4d90-b55d-1fa2e75bea5e",
   "type": "note",
   "content": "The sample is a 64-bit Windows DLL classified as malware with High severity. We assess with moderate confidence that it is a Latrodectus-family downloader and backdoor (attribution confidence 0.70), though engine labels disagree and the family is not confirmed [ev_0014, ev_0018]. Its main risk is code-level capability to fetch files over WinINet, write them to a per-user folder and run them, alongside an HTTP beacon to two configured URLs. No C2 contact, download or task registration was observed in the sandbox run or the packet capture [ev_0013, ev_0015, ev_0017]. Affected hosts should be isolated, any host that loaded or executed this DLL should be investigated, and the two candidate C2 domains should be blocked at the perimeter until a monitored run settles the open questions.",
   "created": "2026-11-06T16:08:05.257869Z",
   "abstract": "Malware \u2014 confidence 0.92",
   "modified": "2026-11-06T16:08:05.257870Z",
